      {
        "id": 56482,
        "name": "Belteshazzar",
        "username": "Belteshazzar",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/e274bd/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-04-02T14:19:08.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Oh, don't get me wrong, we still play Legacy when he/she comes up. It's just hilarious when you get your first and and go, \"Well shoot, all 4 of these are great plays,\" and you feel bad for not playing the three you left in your hand.</p><p>Then there was the time when Grandpappy Legacy, Eternal Haka, and Dark Visionary were taking on the Chairman, and we were taking quite the beating. Visionary went down, and Legacy and Haka both had around 5 HP left, when Legacy got a second Next Evolution out and could make himself immune to melee and projectile (most or all the damage they do) and regain a hit point each turn. The next turn Haka got Haka of Restoration, so we won handily after that. (And then Haka and Legacy proceeded to tease Visionary for getting incapacitated. 'Twas quite silly.)</p>",
