        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/e274bd/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-04-06T13:51:29.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"ketigid\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/9fc29f/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> ketigid:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I've just tried out TLT for the first time. I've got to say it's a very strong supporting power for the rest of the team. None of the team members were in any danger or running out of cards. Tachyon herself was another story. Because she was drawing so many cards, it enhanced her ability to find and play Push the Limits and HUD Goggles and Lightning Reflexes, which in turn consume her cards much faster than before. Tachyon finished the game with only 1 card in hand while the rest of the heroes had tons.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>And I bet her Lightspeed Barrages were hitting like trucks.</p>",
